WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.040
- I feel like we all have a...
Like we're very business...

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:03.873
- It's important.

00:00:03.873 --> 00:00:05.581
- [Kelly] Melanie Griffith,
like working girl right now.

00:00:05.581 --> 00:00:06.414
I like it.

00:00:06.414 --> 00:00:07.331
- It's almost "Big
Business", it's almost...

00:00:07.331 --> 00:00:09.630
- [Kelly] "Big Business",
oh, my God, I love it, yes.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:10.463
I love that one too.

00:00:10.463 --> 00:00:11.482
- I mean, you're nothing
without a power blazer.

00:00:11.482 --> 00:00:12.621
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:00:12.621 --> 00:00:13.454
I'm just nothing.

00:00:13.454 --> 00:00:14.300
- I feel empty.
- Yes.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.180
- How did y'all meet?

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.480
Like when was the first time y'all met?

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.350
- So Kelly, Jessica was performing at a,

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.030
a comedy theater in New York,

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:22.470
called the Upright Citizens Brigade,

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.510
which was an improv theater and...

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.928
- Underneath, a Gristedes Supermarket.

00:00:26.928 --> 00:00:27.761
(women and audience chuckle)

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:28.640
- It's very glamorous.
- Super classy.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.473
- Very glamorous.
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:29.473 --> 00:00:32.160
- And one of my best
friends, Casey Wilson,

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.930
we were performing a show there

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:37.250
and Jessica was already
kind of, an established vet.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:40.552
- And by that, I mean, I
was cleaning the toilets.

00:00:40.552 --> 00:00:41.610
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.650
So that I could get my classes for free.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:44.483
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:44.483 --> 00:00:47.319
And these ladies rolled
in, did none of that.

00:00:47.319 --> 00:00:48.570
(audience chuckles)

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:49.403
- [Kelly] They didn't
have to work for their...

00:00:49.403 --> 00:00:50.870
- Got an 8:00 PM slot.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:52.469
And I'm like, "Who are these..."

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:53.869
(beeping)

00:00:53.869 --> 00:00:54.702
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:00:54.702 --> 00:00:57.189
- [June] I'm so sorry, it's hard...

00:00:57.189 --> 00:00:58.022
- Who are these...
(beeping)

00:00:58.022 --> 00:00:59.650
- It's hard to be this talented,

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:00.929
people just want to lift you up.

00:01:00.929 --> 00:01:03.138
- [Kelly] They just lift
you up, like as you come in.

00:01:03.138 --> 00:01:03.971
- So, we did skip a few steps.

00:01:03.971 --> 00:01:05.770
And, and some of the women in theater

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:07.650
had feelings about that.
- Yeah.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.510
- But Casey and I saw Jessica do a show

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:11.260
and I was like, "I've never seen someone

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:13.220
so funny, so beautiful".

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:17.010
We were obsessed with her
and we locked eyes with her.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.270
And I was like, "She will be our friend".

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:20.103
- Yeah.

00:01:20.103 --> 00:01:21.190
- [June] Casey and I were living together,

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:23.890
we knew Jessica was going to
come out to drinks with us.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:26.430
We were worried about
what we were wearing,

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:29.119
we met her at a bar in the
East Village and then...

00:01:29.119 --> 00:01:29.952
- You wore your power blazer.

00:01:29.952 --> 00:01:31.360
- [June] Of course, I mean I had too.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.193
- [Jessica] Of course.

00:01:32.193 --> 00:01:34.430
- And then Casey, one
of the first questions

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:36.450
out of Casey's mouth to Jessica,

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:37.690
which I was so mad at her about.

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:40.429
She goes, "So, what are
you doing with your pubes?"

00:01:40.429 --> 00:01:41.720
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:44.273
- Oh, my God.
- And I said, "Excuse me?"

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.360
And I was so angry at her.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.150
And I said, we were walking
home in the East Village

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:50.060
and I said, "You blew it, you blew it

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:51.870
with Jessica St. Clair".

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:53.189
- That was when she had me.

00:01:53.189 --> 00:01:54.022
(audience laughs)

00:01:54.022 --> 00:01:54.855
- [Kelly] That was when...

00:01:54.855 --> 00:01:55.820
- That was when she had me because...

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:56.709
- [Kelly] I've found my people.

00:01:56.709 --> 00:01:58.730
(audience laughs)
- I found my people.

00:01:58.730 --> 00:01:59.673
- Oh, my God.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.720
- So, so that's how we met
and then, through the years,

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.560
you know, Jessica and I have
auditioned for shows together

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.870
and been up for a lot of the same roles.

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:13.260
- If she doesn't get
it, I do and vice versa.

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.280
One time she had to drop out

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.810
and they wanted to protect my feelings.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:18.910
They were like, "Do you want this prize?"

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:20.670
Of course, I'm free.
(audience chuckles)

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:22.027
And so, I rolled in and they were like,

00:02:22.027 --> 00:02:23.510
"All the clothes are your size".

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.780
I'm like, "Oh, I know.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:27.028
Because my best friend was
supposed to do this role".

00:02:27.028 --> 00:02:27.861
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:27.861 --> 00:02:29.380
And they were like, "Oh, God, she knows"

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.090
- Okay, wait, I want to
know about "The Deep Dive".

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:34.200
Do you cover important,
life-changing topics like this?

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.795
- Yes, like our bikini lines, absolutely.

00:02:36.795 --> 00:02:38.170
(audience and Kelly chuckle)

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.776
But the podcast is really,

00:02:39.776 --> 00:02:40.650
(June chuckles)

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:45.040
is really about how we are
surviving adult womanhood.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:45.873
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:45.873 --> 00:02:49.960
- Motherhood, our friendships,
aging parents, cancer.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.730
All of the things that life has dealt us.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:53.563
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:53.563 --> 00:02:56.420
- And how so many of our
girlfriends are doing it

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.690
with joy, with laughter.
(audience applauds)

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:00.070
You know, our girls' night...

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:01.657
- [Kelly] You have to laugh.

00:03:01.657 --> 00:03:03.425
- And how we couldn't
do without each other.

00:03:03.425 --> 00:03:04.258
(audience applauds)

00:03:04.258 --> 00:03:05.980
We couldn't survive.
- No.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:07.700
- If you took away our
best friends, we would not,

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:08.930
we would have failure to thrive.

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:10.380
- Yeah, it would just be an empty...

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:11.213
- [Kelly] I'm with you.

00:03:11.213 --> 00:03:12.306
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:12.306 --> 00:03:13.139
(audience applauds)

00:03:13.139 --> 00:03:13.972
- [Kelly] You can never
have too many friends,

00:03:13.972 --> 00:03:15.790
so let's bring out
another pair of besties.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:19.210
One, you can see now in the
latest season of "Woke" on Hulu

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:22.810
and the other, you can see
in "Grand Crew" on NBC.

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:24.740
Together, they also have a podcast.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.425
It's called "Best Friends"
and that's appropriate.

00:03:27.425 --> 00:03:28.590
(audience and Kelly chuckle)

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.050
There's no hiding that.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:33.036
Give it up for Nicole
Byer and Sasheer Zamata.

00:03:33.036 --> 00:03:38.036
(audience applauds)
(upbeat music)

00:03:43.366 --> 00:03:46.366
(audience applauds)

00:03:48.356 --> 00:03:51.825
- [Sasheer] Nice to see you, thank you.

00:03:51.825 --> 00:03:54.894
- [Nicole] It's hard to walk
in these shoes, oh, boy.

00:03:54.894 --> 00:03:57.610
- At this point, Nicole, I
feel like you're a co-host.

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:59.150
I feel like you've been here a few times.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:00.945
- [Nicole] I have, thank
you for having me back.

00:04:00.945 --> 00:04:02.162
- Yes, I know and just had Sasheer on.

00:04:02.162 --> 00:04:02.995
- Yes.
- Yes.

00:04:02.995 --> 00:04:04.444
- And we're literally
talking about like...

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:05.277
- I didn't leave.

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:06.140
- I know, I was like...
- Just stayed here.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.385
- [Kelly] It's a nice dressing room.

00:04:07.385 --> 00:04:08.218
(Kelly chuckles)

00:04:08.218 --> 00:04:10.170
So, like them, y'all
met in improv as well.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:11.530
You were telling me right, last time?

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:12.363
- Yes, yeah.

00:04:12.363 --> 00:04:13.960
Also at the Upright
Citizens Brigade Theater.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.352
- [Kelly] Oh, my God, I didn't
know it was the same one.

00:04:15.352 --> 00:04:16.185
(audience applauds)

00:04:16.185 --> 00:04:17.336
I didn't put that together
and remember, wow.

00:04:17.336 --> 00:04:18.169
(audience applauds)

00:04:18.169 --> 00:04:19.002
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:04:19.002 --> 00:04:20.070
- She was like really cool.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:22.370
She was wearing this
like, turquoise sweater

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:24.190
and a Goldenrod shirt.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:26.073
And she had...
(audience and Nicole laugh)

00:04:26.073 --> 00:04:28.540
And she had a fro and
she was like, so funny.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:30.415
And I was like, "I love her"

00:04:30.415 --> 00:04:32.350
(audience laughs)
- Same.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:34.260
- And I want to be her friend.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:37.550
So then, I like made it a
point to make her my friend

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:38.400
and I won.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.620
- Forced friendships.
- Yes.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:41.816
- We've talked about this.
- Yeah.

00:04:41.816 --> 00:04:44.680
- So, so your podcast is
called "Best Friends".

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:45.697
Was that just, you were like,

00:04:45.697 --> 00:04:47.725
"Yep, that's the name".
(Kelly chuckles)

00:04:47.725 --> 00:04:48.558
Like, you were just..

00:04:48.558 --> 00:04:49.744
- Yeah, we really didn't
think about it too hard.

00:04:49.744 --> 00:04:50.870
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:52.460
- [Kelly] You were like,
"This is what we are".

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:53.293
- This is what we are,

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:54.126
this is what we're going to talk about.

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:55.910
And we talk about friendships on the show.

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:57.460
We talk about our friendship, we catch up

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:00.640
and then, we also answer
people's friendship questions.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:04.480
And I didn't know the
plethora of questions

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:05.840
that could be about about friendship.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:06.750
- Friendship, yeah.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:07.890
- Because it is a relationship

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:08.830
and I think there's so many things,

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:11.770
talking about romantic
relationships or families,

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:13.880
but not a ton about friendship.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:16.990
And so, there's so many people
asking how to make friends,

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:19.250
how to keep them, how to
deepen your friendships.

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.600
And it's, it's been cool,

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:21.880
I feel like it's helped
our friendship too,

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.460
because we get to analyze it more.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.470
- [Kelly] Yeah, and that's a real thing,

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:25.670
I've actually, it was so funny.

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:27.220
I don't see who we're talking to,

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.433
but my sister and I
were talking to somebody

00:05:29.433 --> 00:05:30.607
and they were like,

00:05:30.607 --> 00:05:32.390
"I'm having a hard time,
like finding friends".

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:33.730
And, and she was asking us

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:35.940
and my sister and I were like, "What?"

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:39.210
We'd literally just, we just,
we had just gone to Target

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:41.100
and ran into like two or three women

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.230
that we had full on conversations with.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:44.150
That like, and I was like,

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:45.880
I think it's just hard
if you're an introvert,

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:46.870
like we're extroverts.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:48.020
So like, I think if you're an introvert,

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:49.430
it is a hard thing to kind of, like...

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:51.383
Have y'all always been
like extroverts, like?

00:05:51.383 --> 00:05:52.350
- Yes.
- Oh, yeah.

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:53.520
- Unfortunately, yes.
(audience chuckles)

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.230
- [Kelly] I love, wait, can we just pause

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:56.280
at the idiotic question?

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.303
I just asked women in improv, like, yeah.

00:05:58.303 --> 00:05:59.136
(women chuckle)

00:05:59.136 --> 00:06:00.437
- [Sasheer] I'm an introvert.

00:06:00.437 --> 00:06:01.270
- You are?
- I am.

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:02.103
- See, it's not a dumb question.

00:06:02.103 --> 00:06:03.114
- It's not a dumb question.

00:06:03.114 --> 00:06:03.947
(audience laughs)

00:06:03.947 --> 00:06:04.780
- Yeah, there are no dumb questions,

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:06.160
I found out in fourth grade.
(women chuckle)

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:08.660
So, that's, so that's,
wait, you're an introvert?

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:10.130
- I am, so it is helpful

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:12.330
to have a best friend who's an extrovert,

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.160
because she pulls me
out of my shell a lot.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:14.993
- [Kelly] I would never
have guessed that about you.

00:06:14.993 --> 00:06:17.453
- I'll be like, "Come over
here and get in a waterfall".

00:06:17.453 --> 00:06:19.303
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:06:19.303 --> 00:06:20.380
- [Sasheer] Like, literally.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.840
- Unfortunately for
Jessica and I, you know,

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:24.950
we don't like to go out at the same time,

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:26.880
because we feel like it's
too much for the world.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:27.713
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:06:27.713 --> 00:06:30.500
- Vibrational energy might be
too high and we're too much.

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:32.690
- So, was there a moment
that y'all knew like,

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:35.090
you know, it was your ride or die person?

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:38.522
- Yeah, we, we got dinner pretty early.

00:06:38.522 --> 00:06:39.942
(Sasheer laughs)

00:06:39.942 --> 00:06:41.850
In our, in our friendship.

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:45.230
And Nicole ordered a salad, I can't...

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:46.653
- Okay, it's in my defense, it's like...

00:06:46.653 --> 00:06:48.182
- [Kelly] I love that you're defending it.

00:06:48.182 --> 00:06:49.031
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:06:49.031 --> 00:06:50.031
- [Sasheer] I haven't
even said the thing yet.

00:06:50.031 --> 00:06:51.583
- [Nicole] Okay, but I know
what you're going to say.

00:06:51.583 --> 00:06:53.040
- [Kelly] You're defending
the salad choice.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.000
- Okay, it was, it was a Caesar salad,

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.820
but deconstructed, meaning
I had to assemble it.

00:06:57.820 --> 00:06:59.480
And if I wanted to assemble something,

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:01.212
I could have stayed home.

00:07:01.212 --> 00:07:02.791
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:07:02.791 --> 00:07:04.503
It was, just...
(audience applauds)

00:07:04.503 --> 00:07:06.210
- [Kelly] You had to assemble it?

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:07.970
- Yeah, they brought you the romaine

00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:09.750
and then the, the chicken was over here,

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:11.351
then the croutons are over here.

00:07:11.351 --> 00:07:12.184
- [Kelly] What?

00:07:12.184 --> 00:07:13.040
- And then I said, "Can I have bacon?"

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.823
And then they brought the wrong bacon.

00:07:14.823 --> 00:07:15.656
- They brought the wrong bacon.

00:07:15.656 --> 00:07:18.412
- They brought bits
and I didn't want bits.

00:07:18.412 --> 00:07:20.680
(Nicole laughs)
- But then, and this is like,

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:22.590
like, third time was not the charm.

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:24.080
So she, they had bits,

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.650
and then she wanted a different version,

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:27.120
but they brought like a slab.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.270
And then she...

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:31.204
- It was like, it was
like, a steak of bacon.

00:07:31.204 --> 00:07:32.037
(audience laughs)

00:07:32.037 --> 00:07:34.500
It was so thick and I said,
"This is not the right one".

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.313
And I threw it against the wall.

00:07:36.313 --> 00:07:37.642
- Yeah.
(audience laughs)

00:07:37.642 --> 00:07:39.120
She threw it...
- Oh, my God.

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:39.953
- [Sasheer] On the wall and it just like,

00:07:39.953 --> 00:07:42.367
stuck there for a minute
and like, slid down.

00:07:42.367 --> 00:07:44.550
And we both sat across each other, silent.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:48.170
And I was like, "I'm not going
to say anything right now,

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:49.360
I'm going to wait for
her to say something".

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:50.497
And then, eventually she was like,

00:07:50.497 --> 00:07:51.644
"That was too much, right?"

00:07:51.644 --> 00:07:53.433
And I was like, "Yes".
(audience and Kelly laughs)

00:07:53.433 --> 00:07:54.600
Yes, it was.
(audience laughs)

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:55.945
- Yes, you're crazy.

00:07:55.945 --> 00:07:58.065
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:07:58.065 --> 00:08:00.510
- I was like, "At least
she got there by herself".

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:01.390
- [Kelly] You know why?

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:03.380
Here's the thing, you didn't
really want the salad.

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:05.413
That's the anger, that's
where it started, salads.

00:08:05.413 --> 00:08:06.246
- [Nicole] Oh, no.

00:08:06.246 --> 00:08:07.079
- I don't, yeah, I don't
go out salad for salads.

00:08:07.079 --> 00:08:08.997
- [Nicole] I pay too much
for therapy. (Kelly laughs)

00:08:08.997 --> 00:08:11.105
That was, that is exactly
why I was so angry.

00:08:11.105 --> 00:08:12.090
(Kelly laughs)

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:13.833
It wasn't the bacon that I wanted.

00:08:13.833 --> 00:08:15.540
(Kelly laughs)

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:16.373
- [Kelly] Oh, my God, way to...

00:08:16.373 --> 00:08:18.345
- But they closed, so
I got the last ha-ha.

00:08:18.345 --> 00:08:20.030
(audience laughs)

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:20.863
- [Sasheer] Everyone hated their salads.

00:08:20.863 --> 00:08:23.073
- They made you make, make their food.

00:08:23.073 --> 00:08:23.906
(Kelly chuckles)

00:08:23.906 --> 00:08:26.160
Wait, so what was your ride or die moment?

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:27.190
- Oh, gosh.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:30.210
You know, I, this is a little
bit of a tear-jerker moment,

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:34.350
but I had breast cancer
about six years ago now.

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:38.400
And this one summoned me
in the middle of treatment

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:42.081
to the Four Seasons, where she
was using as her Starbucks.

00:08:42.081 --> 00:08:43.921
(audience chuckles)
- I wasn't welcomed there.

00:08:43.921 --> 00:08:46.480
- We didn't have any money,
she would take a table

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:50.160
and just order sparkling
water and answer emails.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:52.290
So, she said, "Meet me
at the Four Seasons".

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:54.292
And I showed up, and you know...

00:08:54.292 --> 00:08:55.125
- I love this.

00:08:55.125 --> 00:08:56.580
- [Jessica] I said,
"Listen", I go, "June".

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:58.390
And I don't know why I felt like June

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:00.090
was the authority on my health,

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:02.271
when I had some very good doctors.

00:09:02.271 --> 00:09:03.104
(audience laughs)

00:09:03.104 --> 00:09:06.160
But I said, "June, like, do
you think I'm gonna make it?"

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:08.060
And she goes, just like regally,

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:08.930
she probably was in a blazer.

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:12.620
She goes, "Oh I have no, no
question you're gonna make it.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:15.820
What I'm interested in
is your mental health.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:16.653
So, I'm going to"...

00:09:16.653 --> 00:09:18.690
And I feel like she took out a Rolodex,

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:19.950
I know that wasn't true.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:20.783
But she was like,

00:09:20.783 --> 00:09:23.550
"I'm gonna send a multitude
of healers to you".

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:25.170
And I said, "What?"

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:28.120
Cut two, ding dong, like, I'm
going to lay hands on you.

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:29.290
My name's Ethan.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:33.280
Like, I need to sage your house,
like I'm, I do witchcraft.

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:34.770
I was like, "Wait, what?"

00:09:34.770 --> 00:09:36.750
And that's what she did for me.

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:40.480
And, and it was, to know
that, I don't know what it is,

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:41.457
when you ask your best friend,

00:09:41.457 --> 00:09:42.570
"Do you think I'm gonna be okay?"

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:44.260
And they say, yes and you believe them.

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:46.400
It really did give me the courage

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:47.820
to get through the rest of it

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:49.209
and know I'm going to be okay.
(audience applauds)

00:09:49.209 --> 00:09:50.257
And I am.
(audience applauds)

00:09:50.257 --> 00:09:51.090
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.861
- I mean, look.
- She is, better than ever.

00:09:52.861 --> 00:09:55.129
(audience applauds)
Better than ever.

00:09:55.129 --> 00:09:56.933
- Okay, better than ever.
- And listen...

00:09:56.933 --> 00:09:59.230
When you send over 20 healers, like,

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:00.719
they're not all going to be great.

00:10:00.719 --> 00:10:01.718
- [Jessica] They weren't all great.

00:10:01.718 --> 00:10:03.384
(Kelly laughs)
- Some are going to be weird.

00:10:03.384 --> 00:10:05.759
Yes, just the numbers aren't
going to always work out.

00:10:05.759 --> 00:10:08.913
- The numbers are against you,
but someone will work out.

